course: dictionary
lesson: 14809
title: When words claim too much
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what something claims to be, and you must check whether the claim is true. The verb purport means to claim to be or do something, when it may not be true. «The email purports to be from your bank.» The email says it is from your bank, but that does not prove it is. It may be a trick.
explain: Purport is a formal word, so you will meet it in news reports, letters and exams. Look at the words around it for clues. «The man purported to be a doctor, but he had no certificate» tells you he said he was a doctor, and the missing certificate makes you doubt him.
explain: Purport can also be a noun, meaning the general meaning of a text. «The purport of the letter was that the school would close on Friday.» You may read every word of a letter and still need to find its main point. That main point is its purport.
fact: Purport (verb) means to claim to be or do something, when it may not be true.
fact: «Purported» is the past form: «The coin purported to be gold.»
fact: Purport (noun) means the general meaning of a text.
fact: Purport is formal, so it appears in serious writing, news and exams.
fact: Something that purports to be official may be fake, so check before you trust it.
exercise: «The text purported to be a list of facts, but every fact was made up.» What does purported mean here? | Written in a very old language | Proved to be true | Read out loud | *Claimed to be, though it was not true
exercise: «The purport of the story was that kindness wins in the end.» What is the purport of the story? | Its name for the author | Its title in capitals | Its number of pages | *Its general meaning
exercise: A message purports to be from your head teacher and asks for your password. What should you do? | *Check with the school before you trust it | Reply with your home address | Forward it to all your friends | Send your password straight away
test: «The stranger purported to be a police officer.» What does purported suggest? | *He claimed to be one, but he might not be | He was a very tall man | He was a police officer for sure | He arrested a thief
test: Which word means the general meaning of a text? | *purport | purpose | port | portion
exam: A website purports to give free prizes but asks for your bank details. What is the best reaction? | Share it with all your friends | Ask it for more prizes | *Be wary, because the claim may not be true | Trust it and enter your details
